#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d8dc0-98eb-53d0-9e48-3b1c2d7f6308" :question/math-academy-id "e-4508" :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/843dcd4359e4b61eb9715966fbbe6c26363ab5cfc57c55f94b6a41a73ec7feb1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/b9ba240f93ee3ec8c02e9718d62342dca0e0855e24c7b34ed97758a6eb7c46b8.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/id #uuid "422d31ad-8caa-5ce2-a0e0-c905fcc2640d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4509" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/240a1d2f7f93ec808127c9fa1791a77a43fcd7c0c84505540acc81c8b9fbc6e1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/7850cbafc78f2cf2ce14ae7111064bf2f5a029f4d1b97b6d5ebfc09e7126f44e.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed74e342-44d5-5a0d-bdeb-29a74691c7ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} {:answer/id #uuid "e02d476b-35b4-58af-8881-8011cee132f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347170} {:answer/id #uuid "2b946cbc-ba6a-5d77-9082-330ea43c303d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347171} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d043da-6f7b-55c1-b88b-ff8128a46618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347172} {:answer/id #uuid "69ce5340-db64-5350-a1db-996233164143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed74e342-44d5-5a0d-bdeb-29a74691c7ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} :answer-field/id #uuid "004c4b14-e8aa-5080-b660-07820c96dec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c4565b1-69f9-5bcf-baa2-75d567dcc9de" :question/math-academy-id "q-102705" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y=1 \\\\ 2x-3y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65ab0000-86da-5f34-be01-156cdfeb9d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{31}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385848} {:answer/id #uuid "af104d3e-f0ab-59c5-9f0c-71e6a9e7241f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385849} {:answer/id #uuid "650a70e8-e69f-5d62-a110-d20091d57eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{31}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385850} {:answer/id #uuid "4c5e88fd-c399-5822-a231-b8727ddabcef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{31}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385851} {:answer/id #uuid "e5508b89-25cb-556d-b6d5-50c36f18bd9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c5e88fd-c399-5822-a231-b8727ddabcef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{31}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385851} :answer-field/id #uuid "20d59ca7-c121-5094-8135-075100a5c25d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c60618eb-8102-5d29-9fef-37f3fce33d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32026" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=1 \\\\ 8x+3y=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{31}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{31}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1932e59f-ffe6-5cce-bbdd-ca57de490e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385855} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fb7f8d-ff66-5910-b901-e122d7599056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385856} {:answer/id #uuid "cf133ece-1d78-5828-9d00-8f8114cc29f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{27}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385857} {:answer/id #uuid "fd63adfb-8e75-548c-a14d-3cb5b9b450f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385858} {:answer/id #uuid "c37030a2-8c5d-5975-9b98-b7e0e4bc724e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{27}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1932e59f-ffe6-5cce-bbdd-ca57de490e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385855} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddea1231-dc33-5791-ac69-f547edf7820e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d699ebf-34e8-5074-8ce0-17eae71b7321" :question/math-academy-id "q-32028" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-7y=0 \\\\ -3x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 6-(-7)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b6dfa8e-bb8e-524d-bd53-f63ba7e8b63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b6dfa8e-bb8e-524d-bd53-f63ba7e8b63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385862} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ce308bf-4827-5c2b-94f7-b50802e28569" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34f16058-5e85-559d-bfb7-eef60fff2eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34f16058-5e85-559d-bfb7-eef60fff2eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385864} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b3e0fc0-b12c-5827-8882-632ea187a5a2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a069d66f-8264-5533-b2d0-095dd4d884be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a069d66f-8264-5533-b2d0-095dd4d884be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385866} :answer-field/id #uuid "b417bfc8-0ee1-530e-8ab4-8245f8e6e035" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "97708fce-d37c-5254-959a-7a397a10a203" :question/math-academy-id "q-320811" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2y=7-3x \\\\ x+1=-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y=7 \\\\ x+2y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "878aa596-081d-59f0-8f19-5fc123e56583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385869} {:answer/id #uuid "6aec926b-5ad0-5237-b7ae-e2ded3d4c234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aec926b-5ad0-5237-b7ae-e2ded3d4c234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385870} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ced547-f29d-56ef-b6a3-9e22c9b711c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d09df128-fc7f-5abc-86c0-1ee4741f8371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d09df128-fc7f-5abc-86c0-1ee4741f8371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385872} :answer-field/id #uuid "62212952-7c08-55e7-857d-38d9d089a9b2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "babc715a-533c-57eb-a97e-3172f9858bf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "babc715a-533c-57eb-a97e-3172f9858bf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385874} :answer-field/id #uuid "597393b7-fa38-5c17-a6bb-d805291741ef" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "26873337-21a0-5d43-97a3-1553d4d179f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-320842" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3y-2x=5 \\\\ x=-1-4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y=5 \\\\ x+4y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385875 :knowledge-poin