$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9c56f5d-7762-5b58-b737-79569dab6418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385884} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0e98c3-a01e-55dd-9754-51a1c7cca239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9c56f5d-7762-5b58-b737-79569dab6418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385884} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6804b31-8acd-5d8b-93f3-0cee9e33c91d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69afb684-b6b8-5017-9a2f-20eaf8ff1f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69afb684-b6b8-5017-9a2f-20eaf8ff1f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385887} :answer-field/id #uuid "26ea44a2-20e1-5449-82b8-1a28114baf4c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fdef707-4488-547b-a8ec-ac8caaed3fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fdef707-4488-547b-a8ec-ac8caaed3fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385889} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcaf299c-807e-5f1a-b64d-8b1b0c7069b2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16f46ade-26ab-52a6-841d-69b361620358" :question/math-academy-id "q-321437" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x=8 \\\\ 4y=5+3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $5$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $8$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=8 \\\\ -3x+4y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3\\text{ } & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0420cf23-2175-59ad-8af8-e5a5352e4691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0420cf23-2175-59ad-8af8-e5a5352e4691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385892} :answer-field/id #uuid "892f7e39-c35f-5068-9a10-d316cf45943f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e03c2a1-759e-5a63-b677-931b4d7fe0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e03c2a1-759e-5a63-b677-931b4d7fe0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385894} :answer-field/id #uuid "22aa5a52-acff-5a2c-9810-ee716f6cde53" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a24f3df-f623-5cbe-a8a8-ee829c115b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a24f3df-f623-5cbe-a8a8-ee829c115b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385896} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc2cf9d-5713-54aa-8df8-2fa57ab147bf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffd122d4-2c71-543a-bcb5-9e26b267ee22" :question/math-academy-id "q-321438" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7y=-14 \\\\ 2y=5x+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $2$ | $-7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-14$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ | $-7$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-14$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+7y=-14 \\\\ -5x+2y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 2-(-5)\\cdot 7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5b6d23b-d0d4-5dbb-8db7-578185802856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385899} {:answer/id #uuid "1e7f8a25-1786-52d0-ba03-189387e70a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385900} {:answer/id #uuid "32cce108-ac5b-5fea-8383-f90e3ab8c213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385901} {:answer/id #uuid "480bb830-e354-5f9a-adc3-e262845ca9bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385902} {:answer/id #uuid "fe89a93a-2270-5174-821d-e390faba4189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe89a93a-2270-5174-821d-e390faba4189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385903} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e698766-c6c7-5110-82a3-cffb299457b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac75f36c-a5e4-5bd7-8fee-5e3a0c9025f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-72738" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x=3y \\\\ y=-x+1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x-3y=0 \\\\ x+y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot 1-(-3)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
